 !!! Note
     The minimum last stake amount can be configured using `last_stake_amount_min_ratio` - which defaults to 0.5 (50%). This means that the minimum stake amount that's ever used is `stake_amount * 0.5`. This avoids very low stake amounts, that are close to the minimum tradable amount for the pair and can be refused by the exchange.
 
+#### Limiting exposure to a single underlying currency
+
+If several of your pairs are priced against, or settled in, the same underlying currency (for example several BTC-margined futures, or several pairs quoted in the same stablecoin), a large adverse move in that one currency can hit all of those positions at once, even though each trade looked fine in isolation.
+
+`max_currency_exposure` limits the share of your total tradable capital ([tradable balance](#tradable-balance)) that may be committed at the same time to open trades whose pair shares the same underlying (quote/settlement) currency. It is a ratio between `0` and `1`, and is disabled (no limit) by default.
+
+For example, with a tradable capital of 1000 USDT and `max_currency_exposure=0.5`, no more than 500 USDT may be tied up in open trades quoted in USDT at any given time - regardless of `max_open_trades` or `stake_amount`. If opening (or adding to) a trade would push the combined stake for that currency above the limit, the stake is reduced to fit under the limit, or the trade is skipped entirely if even the minimum tradable stake would no longer fit. This applies identically in live/dry-run and in backtesting.
+
+This option can be set globally, or overridden per strategy - see [Strategy Override](#parameters-in-the-strategy).
+
 #### Static stake amount
 
 The `stake_amount` configuration statically configures the amount of stake-currency your bot will use for each trade.
